 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+Session generations live in shared Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md));
+signed cookies carry the member, expiry and generation. Every verification checks the database.
+Install `requirements.txt`, set `DATABASE_URL` on every server and volunteer console to the same database,
+and apply [the schema](../../larder/schema.sql) before deploying this code.
+Database errors propagate: verification must not authenticate a cookie without checking revocation.
+
+## Logout
+
+After a member reported a stolen phone that was still logged in, volunteers needed to end that member's session
+without waiting for inactivity. From a trusted volunteer console, call `larder.sessions.logout(member_id)`.
+Once it returns, all previously issued cookies for that member fail verification on every server, including
+cookies issued before generation tracking was added. Other members remain logged in. Repeating logout is safe,
+and the member can log in again to receive a new cookie.
+
+Only trusted callers may sign cookies or invoke logout; this module does not authorize volunteers.
+Renew a cookie only after successful verification. Requests already authenticated when logout commits can finish.
+Keep generation records permanently: deleting one could make an old cookie valid again.
 
